{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06691 - MONDO_5709",
  "verbalization": "Mepyramine is implicated in the pathogenesis of the Common Cold through a chain of indications that link it to Nasopharyngitis, a condition associated with the cold. The evidence suggests that Mepyramine may exert a therapeutic or pharmacological effect that influences Nasopharyngitis, which in turn is linked to the Common Cold. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple indirect pathways, where Mepyramine is associated with Nasopharyngitis, which is itself linked to the Common Cold via different indications. The shared association with Nasopharyngitis implies a potential role for Mepyramine in modulating inflammatory or immune responses that are characteristic of the condition. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Mepyramine could influence the development or severity of the Common Cold, though the exact nature of this mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
